{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00591",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 7.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Right, Sam, the booking note says you've swallowed a bit of Lego. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.78,
      "end_seconds": 19.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Um... yeah. I swallowed a bit of Lego. A little one. A flat grey piece."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.0,
      "end_seconds": 26.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Okay. Tell me what happened, from the start."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.91,
      "end_seconds": 37.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "I was... um... holding it in my mouth. While I was building a spaceship. And then I sort of... gulped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.1,
      "end_seconds": 44.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Ah, that happens more than you'd think. When was this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.7,
      "end_seconds": 50.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Yesterday. After tea. Or... no, it was before tea, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.01,
      "end_seconds": 59.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "Yesterday, before tea. Did it go down easily, or did it get stuck anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.69,
      "end_seconds": 70.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "It just went down. Straight away. It was a bit... um, weird."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.39,
      "end_seconds": 75.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Any trouble breathing once it had gone down?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.98,
      "end_seconds": 79.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "No. It was fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.5,
      "end_seconds": 85.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Any being sick or vomiting afterwards?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.24,
      "end_seconds": 91.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "No... um, no. I wasn't sick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.64,
      "end_seconds": 98.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Good. And how is your tummy feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.29,
      "end_seconds": 106.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "It's... a bit achy. Not horrible. Just a tummy ache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.99,
      "end_seconds": 113.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Would you call it mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.47,
      "end_seconds": 118.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Mild. I think. Um... yeah, mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.88,
      "end_seconds": 125.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "When did the ache start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.44,
      "end_seconds": 129.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "This morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.32,
      "end_seconds": 136.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Can you point to where it is for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.37,
      "end_seconds": 142.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Here. Um. Round my belly button, like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.75,
      "end_seconds": 151.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "Does anything make it better or worse? Think about eating, or moving around."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.6,
      "end_seconds": 161.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Um... it's a bit worse when I run around. And lying down helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.62,
      "end_seconds": 169.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "Sensible. Now let's check your regular medicines. Do you take anything every day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.2,
      "end_seconds": 177.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Yes. A puffer, I think. And... something for my... um..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.05,
      "end_seconds": 184.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Take your time. What's the puffer for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.57,
      "end_seconds": 191.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "For my asthma. The blue one. Salbutamol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.04,
      "end_seconds": 198.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Good. How much of it, and how often do you use it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.08,
      "end_seconds": 208.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Um... 100 micrograms. When I need it. Mum says it's written on the side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.42,
      "end_seconds": 218.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "That's right, I can see that on your record. What else is there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.22,
      "end_seconds": 226.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "A cream, for my eczema. Hydrocortisone. Once a day, on my elbows."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.78,
      "end_seconds": 230.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "And the last one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.79,
      "end_seconds": 241.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "Um... Movicol. The sachets. For my constipation. Mum makes me have it in orange juice. One sachet a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.42,
      "end_seconds": 248.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "That one's useful today. Keeping it going helps things move along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.21,
      "end_seconds": 255.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Will it help the Lego come out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.33,
      "end_seconds": 279.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.89,
      "text": "It'll certainly not hurt. Hop up on the couch, and I'll have a feel of your tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.94,
      "end_seconds": 289.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Is it going to be cold? Last time the doctor's hands were freezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.9,
      "end_seconds": 315.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "I've warmed them up, promise. Tell me if anything hurts when I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.78,
      "end_seconds": 325.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft, which is what I wanted to feel. You can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.65,
      "end_seconds": 332.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "So what's going to happen to the Lego?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.01,
      "end_seconds": 344.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "Here's what I think. It's small, smooth plastic, so most likely it will pass through on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.25,
      "end_seconds": 348.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "When?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.73,
      "end_seconds": 359.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "Usually within a few days. It comes out with your poo, and you won't feel a thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.62,
      "end_seconds": 368.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Do I have to look in the toilet for it? That's gross."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.64,
      "end_seconds": 380.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "A quick look each day, please, with mum or dad helping. Just so we know it has gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.86,
      "end_seconds": 385.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Um. Okay. I'll make my brother do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.52,
      "end_seconds": 398.46,
      "duration_seconds": 11.94,
      "text": "Ha, nice try. Now, here's what you can do while you wait. Eat normally, with lots of fruit and veg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.8,
      "end_seconds": 402.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "And chips?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.34,
      "end_seconds": 411.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "Sometimes. Drink plenty of water too, and keep taking your Movicol every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.99,
      "end_seconds": 416.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Okay. Can I still build stuff?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.27,
      "end_seconds": 424.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Yes, but not in your mouth. Lego goes in the box and nowhere else."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.69,
      "end_seconds": 428.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Ha. Okay. Um, I won't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.72,
      "end_seconds": 441.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "If the ache gets bad, or you're sick, or you feel hot and unwell, tell mum and come straight in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 442.1,
      "end_seconds": 447.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Okay. I'll tell her. She'll probably tell me anyway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.04,
      "end_seconds": 458.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in three days, to check how things are going."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 460.59,
      "end_seconds": 464.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Um, can it be after school?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.63,
      "end_seconds": 475.36,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "I'll ask reception to find you an afternoon slot. Off you go, Sam, and well done for being so brave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 478.04,
      "end_seconds": 480.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. Bye."
    }
  ]
}
